 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S443-021\", \"clauses\": {\"determine_place_value\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F22\", \"template\": \"What is the {pv_label} of the digit {digit} in {number}?\", \"reasoning\": \"pv_label draws from F01, whose text is place value (in cumulative_vocab); digit runs 0 to 9 and number runs are all 3-digit. The problem asks for the place value of a digit in a 3-digit number.\"}, \"digit_in_3_digit_number\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F21\", \"template\": \"In {number}, what digit is in the {place_name} place?\", \"reasoning\": \"number runs are all 3-digit (102 to 705) and the question asks for the digit of that number, so the object of the clause is addressed.\"}, \"determine_value_of_digit\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F18\", \"template\": \"In the number {number}, the value of the digit {digit} in the {place} place is {fill_value}\", \"reasoning\": \"F18 is a true/false statement about the value of a digit in a 3-digit number, so it addresses the clause. Producibility holds even though F18 is a failing family in Rule 1, which is why the clause verdict is independent of that finding.\"}, \"determine_digit_given_place_value\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F21\", \"template\": \"In {number}, what digit is in the {place_name} place?\", \"reasoning\": \"place_name is one of hundreds, ones, tens (repeats the generated place name), and the question asks for the digit given that place value.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F06\", \"F07\", \"F13\", \"F14\", \"F15\", \"F18\", \"F19\", \"F20\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Count from the right: {relevant_places}.\", \"Look at the digits of {number} from the right: {relevant_places}.\", \"Multiply it by its place: {digit} × {v} = {value}.\", \"{p0}\", \"{p0}, {p1}\", \"{p0}, {p1}, {p2}\", \"In the number {number}, the value of the digit {digit} in the {place} place is {fill_value}\", \"{question_text} The answer is {fill_value}.\", \"{statement}. True or False?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 prints the concept multiplication, which is in NOT_YET_KNOWN, through the verb Multiply and the times sign; its v slot also draws 1000 from PLACE_VALUES, a place no 3-digit number has. F13, F14 and F15 draw from PLACE_NAMES, which includes thousands; no 3-digit number has that place, and F13 is also a correct_answer and mcq_options family, so a keyed answer can be thousands. F03 and F06 print F13 to F15 inside hints, so they carry the same fault. F18 hard-codes the word value in its template; the lc's gate for value prints worth and never prints value, and value is not in cumulative_vocab. F18's fill_value distractor members (including 1, 2, 5, 6, 60 and 500) are not tied to the digit, place or number slots, so a distractor can equal the true value for the digit and place drawn and be labelled false. F19 has the same untied distractor problem (digits 0 to 9 among its distractor members, against a question that may have a digit answer). F20 prints F18 and F19 inside True or False. Not failing: F23 prints the doubled word in, in (ungrammatical but readable); F19 ends with a period that F20 doubles (typographic); F04 reads awkwardly (the tens place value of a number) but is not wrong. F01, F02, F05, F08 to F12, F16, F17, F21 and F22 pass on Rule 1.\"}",
